.TH ACTIVITYTRACK 1 "November 2026" "activitytrack 0.9.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
activitytrack \- ActivityTrack from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B activitytrack
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B activitytrack \-i
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B activitytrack
records activities and works the to-dos of ActivityTrack: the same data as
the Android app, the web server ActivityTrack Web and the desktop tray
application, which it shares on this PC (data folder, pairing, token).
Every change is pushed to the server at the end of the command; without a
network it leaves with the next sync. Without a command it shows the
activities running.
.PP
Activities and to-dos are named by the first characters of the id the
listings show (at least 3). Times are
.I HH:MM
(today) or a day and a time; days are
.IR 2026-11-03 ,
.IR 3/11 ,
.IR oggi ,
.IR domani
or
.IR ieri .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-interactive
Numbered lists to choose from, in colour when the terminal supports it.
Where a question shows the present value in brackets, an empty answer keeps
it and
.B \-
clears it.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the result as JSON, for scripts. After a change the object has a
.B sync
field: the state of the sync that followed (ok, idle, offline, failed,
revoked, incompatible), unpaired when the PC is not paired, null with
.BR \-\-no\-sync .
An error is an object with
.B error
(the message) and
.BR code .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sync
Do not sync after a change.
.TP
.BI \-\-data " folder"
Another data folder than the shared one.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
The activities running and the state of the sync.
.TP
.BR start " [\fIdescription\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIclient\fR] [\fB\-\-company\fR \fIc\fR] [\fB\-\-role\fR \fIr\fR] [\fB\-t\fR \fItags\fR] [\fB\-\-travel\fR] [\fB\-\-todo\fR \fIid\fR] [\fB\-\-at\fR \fItime\fR] [\fB\-\-until\fR \fItime\fR] [\fB\-\-others\fR suspend|stop|keep]"
Start an activity. A client typed that does not exist becomes a new one,
when the policy allows it.
.B \-\-until
records an activity already done. The activities running are suspended,
unless
.BR \-\-others .
.TP
.BR pause ", " resume ", " travel ", " suspend ", " stop " [\fIid\fR] [\fB\-\-at\fR \fItime\fR]"
A command on the activity running (or the one named).
.TP
.BR complete " \fIid\fR [\fB\-d\fR \fIdescription\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIclient\fR] [\fB\-\-empty\fR] [\fB\-\-todo\-done\fR]"
Complete an activity whose details were missing.
.TP
.BR edit " \fIid\fR [\fB\-d\fR] [\fB\-c\fR] [\fB\-\-company\fR] [\fB\-\-role\fR] [\fB\-\-locality\fR] [\fB\-\-notes\fR] [\fB\-t\fR]"
Change an activity.
.TP
.BR reopen ", " delete " \fIid\fR"
Reopen a closed activity; delete one (asks, unless \fB\-\-yes\fR; with
\fB\-\-json\fR it does not ask).
.TP
.BR list " [\fB\-\-period\fR today|24h|3d|7d|30d|all] [\fB\-\-show\fR todo,missing,done,ignored] [\fB\-\-company\fR \fIid\fR] [\fB\-\-tag\fR \fItag\fR]"
The Home list of the app: to-dos and stopped activities.
.TP
.BR "todo list" ", " "todo add" " \fItitle\fR [\fB\-c\fR] [\fB\-\-due\fR \fIday\fR [\fItime\fR]] [\fB\-\-plan\fR \fIday\fR [\fItime\fR [\fIminutes\fR]]] [\fB\-\-priority\fR 1-5] [\fB\-\-notes\fR] [\fB\-\-refs\fR]"
The to-dos; a new one.
.TP
.BR "todo edit" ", " start ", " done ", " ignore ", " reopen ", " postpone " [\fIminutes\fR], " delete " \fIid\fR"
Work a to-do.
.B todo delete
does not ask for a confirmation.
.TP
.B sync
Sync now.
.TP
.BR pair " [\fIlink\fR|\fB\-\fR]"
Pair this PC with an ActivityTrack Web server: the link of the web's
Dispositivi page. Without it, the link is asked and not shown while it is
pasted: the way to prefer, as a link on the command line stays in the
shell's history and, while the command runs, in the list of the processes,
until its code is used or expires.
.B \-
reads it from the standard input, as does a standard input that is not a
terminal.
.TP
.BR update " [\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-download\fR] [\fB\-\-channel\fR \fIchannel\fR]"
Ask the server this PC is paired with whether there is a newer version.
The server's announcement is signed; it is accepted only with the key of
the pairing link, so a PC paired with an older link (without the key), or
an announcement signed by another key, is refused with the reason.
.B \-\-check
(the default) only tells; the exit status is 10 when a newer version is
there.
.B \-\-download
fetches the package from the server and checks its SHA-256. An installation
made by the package manager is told of the new version but is
.I not
offered the download: the package manager updates it.
.B \-\-channel
adds a channel to prod for this run (beta, test, dev; may be repeated); a
policy that fixes the betas off keeps beta out. The setting that turns the
check off is the desktop's (Impostazioni, Generale) and is respected.
.TP
.B unpair
Unpair; the data stay.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
No colours.
.TP
.BR LANG ", " LC_ALL
The language (it, en, de, es), unless the policy fixes it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/activitytrack/
The data shared with the desktop application.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 done; 1 refused or failed (the message says why, without a traceback:
also for data that cannot be read); 2 wrong usage; 10
.B update
found a newer version.
.SH AUTHOR
The ActivityTrack contributors, https://gitlab.com/activitytrack/activitytrack-cli
